# No catch-all rewrite here, on purpose.
#
# This file used to send every unknown path to the app with `/* /index.html 200`.
# That answered anything - /.env, /nope, a missing /assets/index-*.js - with the
# home page and a 200. Crawlers saw pages that do not exist, and on 2026-11-25 a
# script requested mid-deploy was answered with HTML that the edge then cached
# as the script, so the site stopped running in browsers.
#
# Every real route has its own prerendered HTML file (seo/prerender.mts), so
# none of them needs the rewrite. Unknown paths get 404.html or en/404.html with
# a real 404 status: Cloudflare Pages does that whenever a top-level 404.html
# exists and no rule here catches the path first. Do not add `/*` back.

# Hermes was renamed Trinity Agent on 2026-11-25; old links keep working.
/projects/hermes /projects/trinity-agent 301
/en/projects/hermes /en/projects/trinity-agent 301
